  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "The killer was Zane Swain. The touch faltered twice. Fides tripped about the second minute of the touch; the green hand's own trip — a new hand's stumble convicts nobody, and the tower thinks no worse of it. But Spes hung late where the method wanted her elsewhere, and no custom excuses it; that rope was in Zane Swain's keeping, and the hands that should have held it were free about the second minute of the touch. Wat Frew did not survive the office.\n\nAs to the why of it: Of Zane Swain, the playbill says: Zane Swain — a footman, twin to Fifi; correct in all things, fond of the rules. Of Wat Frew: Captain Wat Frew — a sea-captain of elastic accounts; owed money by half the company.\n\nThe tower proved every pair of hands but one.",
